leo Fields (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Louisiana's 6th District is an open seat after Democrat Cleo Fields chose to run for state senate instead of defending it. Redistricting made the district substantially more Republican, with a 16-point Republican lean on the partisan baseline. State Senator Blake Miguez dominates fundraising with $6.6 million raised and $2 million on hand, far ahead of rival Republican Rick Edmonds and the Democratic field. Democrat Lindsay Garcia has raised only about $65,000, and no outside spending has materialized for either side.\n\nThe race has drawn attention mainly for the heated Republican primary, with Miguez and Edmonds trading residency accusations and Miguez's endorsements drawing criticism. A late-summer survey showed Democrats stuck near 27 percent in a hypothetical matchup, and prediction markets price the Republican at roughly 93 percent. The general election is expected to be safely Republican, with the real contest decided in the primary.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.024, "margin": -16.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0303, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0192, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0083, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0276, "margin": -17.0}]}